-- הסכם קיבוצי — טבלת השכר למורים, תוספת 2011 (25.1.2011): the first part of
-- the 2011 public-sector cost framework for teaching employees in the
-- State's service, until 31.12.2012. From 1.1.2011, 2.25%: for Ofek Hadash
-- teachers and for the supervision and headquarters staff of the agreement
-- of 5.7.2010, the salary tables rise by it, and the updated tables are its
-- thirty annexes (א1'–א22' and ב1'–ב8'); for the teachers off the reform, a
-- new "2011 supplement" of 2.25% on the combined salary with the 2001 and
-- 2008 supplements, and the shekel supplements raised by it. A one-time
-- grant by two Treasury circulars, and the exhaustion of the base
-- agreement's §155(א) for this part of the framework.
--
-- The annexes are DATA: every table is written here cell for cell as the
-- corpus publishes it, in the base agreement's §46 shape (a row is a list of
-- `grade cell`), so §46's and §71's placement rules run on them unchanged.
-- Where the base agreement gives the rule a table should follow — the first
-- deputies' tables at 75% of the principals' (§92(א), §98(ב)), the
-- conversion tables as the same tables with intermediate grades (§46(א),
-- §71(א), §98(א)) — the checks at the end run it over every cell, and so do
-- the steps each table prints in its own header row and column. The tables
-- in force before 1.1.2011 are not in the corpus, so the 2.25% itself
-- cannot be checked cell by cell here.
--
-- The base agreement of 25.12.2008 is imported where this agreement applies
-- or amends it: §35's table update (the 2.25% is one more update of the
-- tables, dated), §46's grade cell and placement, §92's 75%, and §155(א),
-- which §6 exhausts for this part. The framework agreement of 12.1.2011
-- is encoded at l4/agreements/framework/2011-01-12_framework-agreement_public-sector_tosefet-2011.l4
-- and not imported here (what this agreement takes from it, it states in
-- its own words); the supervision agreement of 5.7.2010 is not in the
-- corpus. Of the Treasury circulars of §5, הע 2010-1-58 the corpus holds
-- as part of the framework agreement's annex ב' (with הע 2010-1-47 of
-- 15.11.2010, not the הע 2010-1-48 of 16.11.2010 §5 names); 2010-1-48 it
-- does not hold. Annexes ג1'–ג2', which §5 names, are not in the document
-- as the corpus holds it: named inputs where a rule needs them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `base-agreement-35`
IMPORT `base-agreement-46`
IMPORT `base-agreement-92`
IMPORT `base-agreement-155`

-- A salary month, counted as month m of year y.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary month` y m IS
    y TIMES 12 PLUS m

§ `הסכם תוספת 2011, החלק הראשון — 25.1.2011`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 A handwritten annex mark on the copy; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 A fax header; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 A fax header; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The Registrar's stamp: registered on 18.11.2013 as no. 213/2013; no rule of the agreement.

-- The day of signing, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p6
`the day this agreement was signed` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 25 1 2011

-- The parties: the State, by the Treasury's wages commissioner and the
-- Ministry of Education's director-general, and the teachers' union, by its
-- secretary-general; the base agreement's own parties (`Party`).
@ref akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11
`the parties` MEANS LIST `the State`, `the teachers' union`

-- akn:preamble/p9 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 "On the other side"; no rule.

-- The recitals: the base agreement (25.12.08) bound the parties to negotiate
-- applying to teaching employees in the State's service the cost of
-- framework agreements signed later (its §155(א)); the framework agreement
-- of 12.1.2011 was signed; they negotiated; and they agreed on applying part
-- of the cost framework its §4 sets ("מסגרת עלות התוספות"). A framework
-- agreement's cost is one of the matters §155 keeps open.
@ref akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15 akn:preamble/p16
`the framework agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2011

@ref akn:preamble/p13
`the base agreement keeps a framework agreement's cost open` MEANS
    `may be negotiated` `the cost of a framework agreement`

-- akn:preamble/p17 A recital: the parties wish to anchor their agreement in a collective agreement; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p18 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p19 A fax footer; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p20 A fax header; no rule.

§§ `1 המבוא והנספחים`

-- The preamble and the annexes are an inseparable part of the agreement:
-- the thirty tables below are the agreement's, as §4(ב)(1) applies them.
@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1/p1
DECLARE `part of the agreement` IS ONE OF
    `the preamble`
    `the body of the agreement`
    `an annex`

GIVEN p IS A `part of the agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an inseparable part of the agreement` p IF
    TRUE

§§ `2 תקופת ההסכם`

-- For the period until 31.12.2012; the text names no first day, and the
-- rules below run from 1.1.2011 (§4).
@ref akn:art_2 akn:art_2/p1
`the agreement runs until` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2012

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is in its period on` d IF
        d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011)
    AND d `is on or before` `the agreement runs until`

§§ `3 תחולת ההסכם`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as this agreement asks about him.
DECLARE `employee` HAS
    `graded on the teaching-staff grade`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed in the State's service`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `terms`                               IS A `terms of employment`

@desc The terms an employee is employed under, as §4(ב) divides them.
DECLARE `terms of employment` IS ONE OF
    `the reform's terms`
    @desc a supervision or headquarters role under the collective agreement of 5.7.2010
    `a supervision or headquarters role`
    @desc the collective agreements of employment not under the reform
    `the terms off the reform`

-- Every employee graded on the teaching-staff grade and employed in the
-- State's service ("עובדי הוראה").
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3/p1
GIVEN e IS AN `employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this agreement applies to` e IF
        e's `graded on the teaching-staff grade`
    AND e's `employed in the State's service`

§§ `4 יישום עלות של 2.25%`

-- (א): from 1.1.2011 the first part of the cost framework, set by §5.1.1
-- of the framework agreement, is allocated: 2.25%.
@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_4__para_a
`the first part of the cost framework` MEANS 2.25%

@ref akn:art_4__para_a
`the allocation starts on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011

-- (ב): the allocation is made as (1) and (2) say, by the employee's terms.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b
DECLARE `way of the allocation` IS ONE OF
    `the salary tables updated`
    `the 2011 supplement and the shekel supplements updated`

GIVEN e IS AN `employee`
GIVETH A MAYBE `way of the allocation`
DECIDE `how the allocation reaches` e IS
    IF NOT `this agreement applies to` e
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER e's `terms`
         WHEN `the reform's terms` THEN JUST `the salary tables updated`
         WHEN `a supervision or headquarters role` THEN JUST `the salary tables updated`
         WHEN `the terms off the reform` THEN JUST `the 2011 supplement and the shekel supplements updated`

-- (ב)(1): for the reform's teachers, and for the supervision and
-- headquarters staff of the agreement of 5.7.2010, the salary tables are
-- updated by 2.25%: one more update of the base agreement's tables (§35(ב)),
-- dated 1.1.2011 — the uniform rise of the tables that §155(א)(1) names.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_1
`the 2011 table update rate` MEANS 2.25%

@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_1
`the 2011 table update` MEANS
    `table update` WITH
        `from` IS `the allocation starts on`
        `rate` IS `the 2011 table update rate`

-- The updated tables are attached: א1'–א22' for the reform's teachers,
-- ב1'–ב8' for the supervision and headquarters staff (below).
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_1/p3
GIVEN t IS A `terms of employment`
GIVETH A LIST OF `salary table`
DECIDE `the updated tables for` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `the reform's terms` THEN `annexes א1'–א22'`
    WHEN `a supervision or headquarters role` THEN `annexes ב1'–ב8'`
    WHEN `the terms off the reform` THEN EMPTY

-- (ב)(2): for the teachers off the reform (and, the text adds, not in a
-- supervision or headquarters role).
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is off the reform under 4(ב)(2)` e IF
        `this agreement applies to` e
    AND e's `terms` EQUALS `the terms off the reform`

-- (ב)(2)(א): from 1.1.2011 a new supplement of 2.25%, on the combined
-- salary, the 2001 supplement and the 2008 supplement ("תוספת 2011"). The
-- 2001 and 2008 supplements are computed under their own instruments, as
-- (ב) orders below: inputs here. No rounding is stated (convention
-- rounding.default).
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_a
`the 2011 supplement rate` MEANS 2.25%

@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_a
GIVEN e IS AN `employee`
      `the combined salary`  IS A NUMBER
      `the 2001 supplement`  IS A NUMBER @desc computed on a salary without the 2008 or the 2011 supplement (§4(ב)(2)(ב))
      `the 2008 supplement`  IS A NUMBER @desc computed on a salary without the 2011 supplement (§4(ב)(2)(ב))
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2011 supplement amount` e `the combined salary` `the 2001 supplement` `the 2008 supplement` d IS
    IF `is off the reform under 4(ב)(2)` e AND d `is on or after` `the allocation starts on`
    THEN `the 2011 supplement rate` TIMES (`the combined salary` PLUS `the 2001 supplement` PLUS `the 2008 supplement`)
    ELSE 0

-- (ב)(2)(ב): the order of computing: the 2001 supplement first (on a base
-- with neither later supplement), then the 2008 supplement (on a base
-- without the 2011 supplement), then the 2011 supplement.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_b
DECLARE `supplement computed` IS ONE OF
    `the 2001 supplement computed`
    `the 2008 supplement computed`
    `the 2011 supplement computed`

@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_b
`the order of computing` MEANS
    LIST `the 2001 supplement computed`, `the 2008 supplement computed`, `the 2011 supplement computed`

-- (ב)(2)(ג)–(ד): not toward the top-up to the minimum wage; salary for
-- every purpose, and toward the percentage supplements computed from the
-- combined salary save the 2001 and 2008 supplements, the hour value,
-- severance pay, pensions, and contributions to a pension, the study fund,
-- the Dafna fund and every other contribution or deduction customary on the
-- combined salary.
@desc A use a salary component may count toward, as §4(ב)(2)(ג)–(ה) list them.
DECLARE `salary use` IS ONE OF
    `the top-up to the minimum wage`
    `percentage supplements computed from the combined salary`
    `the 2001 supplement's base`
    `the 2008 supplement's base`
    `the hour value`
    `severance pay under the Severance Pay Law`
    `pensions`
    `contributions to a pension, the study fund and the Dafna fund`
    `every other contribution or deduction customary on the combined salary`
    `the determining salary under section 8 of the State Service (Pensions) Law`

@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_c akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_d
GIVEN u IS A `salary use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2011 supplement counts toward` u IF
    CONSIDER u
    WHEN `the top-up to the minimum wage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the 2001 supplement's base` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the 2008 supplement's base` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (ב)(2)(ה): the government declares that, under §8 of the State Service
-- (Pensions) Law, the 2011 supplement counts in the determining salary — a
-- declaration, which the rule above already carries.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_e
`the government's declaration on the determining salary` MEANS
    `the 2011 supplement counts toward` `the determining salary under section 8 of the State Service (Pensions) Law`

-- (ב)(2)(ו) with its definition: the shekel supplements are updated by
-- 2.25% from 1.1.2011. They are every shekel supplement paid to teaching
-- employees on the teaching-staff grade under the agreements off the reform
-- on the eve of signing, save those not updated by the cost-of-living
-- agreements (having another mechanism) and the minimum-wage top-up.
@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_f
`the shekel supplements' update rate` MEANS 2.25%

@desc A shekel supplement as the definition of §4(ב)(2) asks about it.
DECLARE `shekel supplement` HAS
    `paid on the eve of signing under the agreements off the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc false where it has another updating mechanism
    `is the top-up to the minimum wage`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount on 31.12.2010`                                            IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2/p2
GIVEN s IS A `shekel supplement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is one of the shekel supplements` s IF
        s's `paid on the eve of signing under the agreements off the reform`
    AND s's `updated by the cost-of-living agreements`
    AND NOT s's `is the top-up to the minimum wage`

@ref akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_f
GIVEN s IS A `shekel supplement`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel supplement on` s d IS
    IF `is one of the shekel supplements` s AND d `is on or after` `the allocation starts on`
    THEN (s's `amount on 31.12.2010`) `increased by` `the shekel supplements' update rate`
    ELSE s's `amount on 31.12.2010`

-- akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_f/p2 A fax footer; no rule.
-- akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2__cls_f/p3 A fax header; no rule.

DECLARE `agreement action` IS ONE OF
    `pay what section 4 gives`

-- (ג): carried out with the January 2011 salary, and at the latest with
-- February's (convention dates.salary-month).
@ref akn:art_4__para_c
`carried out with the salary of` MEANS `salary month` 2011 1
@ref akn:art_4__para_c
`at the latest with the salary of` MEANS `salary month` 2011 2

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `agreement action`
DECIDE `carrying out section 4` IS
    PARTY `the State` MUST `pay what section 4 gives`
    LEST BREACH BY `the State` BECAUSE "section 4(ג): carried out with February 2011's salary at the latest"

GIVEN `the salary month paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 is carried out in time` `the salary month paid` IF
    `the salary month paid` AT MOST `at the latest with the salary of`

§§ `5 מענק חד פעמי`
    @ref akn:art_5 akn:art_5/p1
    GIVEN `the one-time grant under the wages commissioner's circulars` IS A FUNCTION FROM `employee` TO NUMBER

-- A one-time grant to the teaching employees, by the wages commissioner's
-- circulars הע 2010-1-48 (16.11.2010) and הע 2010-1-58 (19.12.2010), said to
-- be annexes ג1'–ג2'. The annexes are not in the document as the corpus
-- holds it; of the circulars the corpus holds only הע 2010-1-58, inside
-- the framework agreement of 12.1.2011's annex ב', where it amends הע
-- 2010-1-47, not the הע 2010-1-48 §5 names, which the corpus does not
-- hold: the grant is an input.

GIVEN e IS AN `employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the one-time grant` e IS
    IF `this agreement applies to` e
    THEN `the one-time grant under the wages commissioner's circulars` e
    ELSE 0

§§ `6 מיצוי תביעות`

-- The agreement fully exhausts the base agreement's §155(א) for the first
-- part of the cost framework (2.25%, §5.1.1 of the framework agreement),
-- for the one-time grant (its §5.2) and for its §9; for the rest of the
-- cost framework §155(א) still governs.
@ref akn:art_6 akn:art_6/p1 akn:art_6/p2
DECLARE `part of the framework` IS ONE OF
    `the first part of the cost framework (2.25%)`
    `the one-time grant of section 5.2`
    `section 9 of the framework agreement`
    `the rest of the cost framework`

GIVEN p IS A `part of the framework`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 155(א) still governs` p IF
    p EQUALS `the rest of the cost framework`

-- How a part is applied: what this agreement settles, as the parties
-- agreed; the rest, as the base agreement's §155(א) says.
@ref akn:art_6/p2
GIVEN p IS A `part of the framework`
      `days since the framework agreement was signed` IS A NUMBER
      `the parties agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `way of applying a framework cost`
DECIDE `how a part of the framework is applied` p `days since the framework agreement was signed` `the parties agreed` `under the reform` IS
    IF `section 155(א) still governs` p
    THEN `how a framework cost is applied` `days since the framework agreement was signed` `the parties agreed` `under the reform`
    ELSE `as the parties agreed`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 "In witness whereof"; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p3 The union's stamp; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/t1 The parties' signature headings; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p4 The Treasury's file number; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p5 A fax footer; no rule.
-- THE ANNEXES. Thirty tables, each written below cell for cell as the
-- corpus publishes it. A table is its rating code, the grade steps its
-- header row prints, and its rows; a row is its place among the printed
-- rows, the label it prints at its head (a teachers' table's seniority, a
-- principals' or deputies' table's complexity level), the step it prints
-- beside the label (a rate over the row above, or, in a principals' or
-- deputies' table, shekels over the level below), and its cells — the base
-- agreement's §46 `grade cell`s, so §46's and §71's placement rules run on
-- a row unchanged. A blank cell (a grade the seniority does not reach) is
-- not in its row; neither is a cell the corpus reads [לא קריא], and the
-- table says so where it is.
--
-- The principals' and deputies' tables print their grades as letters; the
-- base agreement numbers them ("הדרגה המקסימאלית (4)", §71(ג), §98(ג)):
-- א is 1, ב 2, ג 3, ד 4, and an intermediate א+ 1.5, ב+ 2.5, ג+ 3.5.

@desc What a table prints beside a row's label: the step from the row above.
DECLARE `printed step` IS ONE OF
    `no step`
    `a rate` HAS `the step's rate` IS A NUMBER
    `shekels` HAS `the step in shekels` IS A NUMBER

@desc One printed row of a salary table.
DECLARE `table row` HAS
    `row place` IS A NUMBER        @desc its place among the table's printed rows, from the top
    `row label` IS A MAYBE NUMBER  @desc the seniority or complexity level printed at its head; NOTHING where the corpus reads it [לא קריא] or the table prints none
    `row step`  IS A `printed step`
    `row cells` IS A LIST OF `grade cell`

GIVEN p  IS A NUMBER
      l  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      s  IS A `printed step`
      cs IS A LIST OF `grade cell`
GIVETH A `table row`
DECIDE `row` p l s cs IS
    `table row` WITH
        `row place` IS p
        `row label` IS l
        `row step`  IS s
        `row cells` IS cs

@desc A grade's step over the grade before it, as a table's header row prints it.
DECLARE `grade step` HAS
    `the stepped grade` IS A NUMBER
    `the grade's rate`  IS A NUMBER

@desc A salary table annexed to the agreement.
DECLARE `salary table` HAS
    `rating code` IS A NUMBER @desc קוד דירוג, as the table's title prints it
    `grade steps` IS A LIST OF `grade step`
    `rows`        IS A LIST OF `table row`

-- Every annexed table is "updated from 1.1.2011", as each prints under it
-- (the four new supervision tables share a page with their conversion
-- tables and print it once, under those).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 akn:att_2__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1/p2 akn:att_7__hc_1/p2 akn:att_8__hc_1/p2 akn:att_9__hc_1/p2 akn:att_10__hc_1/p2 akn:att_11__hc_1/p2 akn:att_12__hc_1/p2 akn:att_13__hc_1/p2 akn:att_14__hc_1/p2 akn:att_15__hc_1/p2 akn:att_16__hc_1/p2 akn:att_17__hc_1/p2 akn:att_18__hc_1/p2 akn:att_19__hc_1/p2 akn:att_20__hc_1/p2 akn:att_21__hc_1/p2 akn:att_22__hc_1/p2 akn:att_24__hc_1/p2 akn:att_26__hc_1/p2 akn:att_28__hc_1/p2 akn:att_30__hc_1/p2
`the annexed tables are updated from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011

-- A row's cell at a grade, and a table's cell at a printed row and grade.
GIVEN g IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF `grade cell`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the pay at grade` g cs IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's grade EQUALS g) cs
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (c's pay)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

GIVEN t IS A `salary table`, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade cell`
DECIDE `the cells of row` t p IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row cells`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row place` EQUALS p) (t's `rows`)))

GIVEN t IS A `salary table`, p IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the cell of` t p g IS
    `the pay at grade` g (`the cells of row` t p)

-- A table's row by the label it prints: the seniority row of a teachers'
-- conversion table, the complexity level of a principals' table. Annexes
-- א1' and א2' print no readable label, so they are read by place (the
-- checks below set them beside א3' and א4', which label every row).
GIVEN t IS A `salary table`, l IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade cell`
DECIDE `the row labelled` t l IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row cells`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row label` EQUALS JUST l) (t's `rows`)))

-- The table salary on a day: the cell at the label's row and the grade,
-- from the day the tables are updated.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, t IS A `salary table`, l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the table salary on` d t l g IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the annexed tables are updated from`
    THEN `the pay at grade` g (`the row labelled` t l)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `נספחים א1'–א7' טבלאות השכר של המורים`

-- א1': טבלת השכר למורים בעלי תואר BA (קוד דירוג 101)
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1 akn:att_1__hc_1/t1
`annex א1'` MEANS
    `salary table` WITH
        `rating code` IS 101
        `grade steps` IS LIST `grade step` 2 (7.5%), `grade step` 3 (7.5%), `grade step` 4 (7.5%), `grade step` 5 (7.5%), `grade step` 6 (7.5%), `grade step` 7 (8.5%), `grade step` 8 (8.5%), `grade step` 9 (8.5%)
        -- printed row 1, grade 1: the corpus reads the cell [לא קריא]; the row gives no value for it
        -- every seniority label, and the header's corner cells, are [לא קריא] in the corpus: a row carries NOTHING for its seniority
        `rows` IS LIST
            `row` 1 NOTHING `no step` EMPTY,
            `row` 2 NOTHING (`a rate` (2%)) (LIST `cell` 1 5693.46),
            `row` 3 NOTHING (`a rate` (2%)) (LIST `cell` 1 5807.33, `cell` 2 6242.88),
            `row` 4 NOTHING (`a rate` (2%)) (LIST `cell` 1 5923.48, `cell` 2 6367.74),
            `row` 5 NOTHING (`a rate` (2%)) (LIST `cell` 1 6041.95, `cell` 2 6495.10, `cell` 3 6982.23),
